 "narrative": "All estimates are signed to the registered claim direction, so positive estimates support the claimed direction and negative estimates oppose it. The named binary research markers do not show scientifically meaningful main effects in this dataset. feature_007 (R1, signed estimate -0.019) and feature_058 (R2, +0.008) are essentially null, and feature_015 (R3, -0.039) is opposite to its claimed protective direction but far too small to accept. Their associated signature interactions are also weak: elevated feature_038 does not clearly amplify feature_007-associated stronger dependency (R4, -0.017); elevated feature_018 has a small positive attenuation estimate for feature_058 (R5, +0.063, CI to 0.187) but its point estimate is well below the 0.15-unit threshold; elevated feature_036 does not clearly amplify feature_015 (R6, +0.016). Clinical or numeric modifier interactions are not supported: older-age interaction with feature_007 is negative/unsupported (R7, -0.083), feature_012 interaction with feature_058 is only +0.063 (R8, CI to 0.187), feature_040 interaction with feature_015 is opposite (R9, -0.073), and feature_058 co-occurrence does not amplify feature_007 (R10, -0.027). Broad nominal check feature_024 level_002 versus level_001 is null (R11, -0.016). The only informative signal is feature_003 versus 0 (R12): signed estimate +0.139 (95% CI 0.065 to 0.213) for direction -1, corresponding to lower composite dependency score in feature_003-positive cases by about 0.139 units. This is close to, but does not exceed, the 0.15-unit threshold; the interval includes values both below and above the threshold. Given that this emerged among 12 exploratory comparisons, that feature_003 has no prior biological justification in the supplied study description, and that the point estimate is below threshold, I cannot accept it. I mark H12 unresolved and active and request independent validation. H5 and H8 are left unresolved but deferred because their upper CIs cross the threshold but point estimates are too small and biologically weak to justify immediate follow-up before validating H12. All other claims are rejected as unsupported in this dataset. Alternative explanations for H12 include a false positive, a true but subthreshold effect, residual confounding by correlated features, or chance distribution of feature_003; the proposed follow-ups only estimate feature_003 within subgroups or modify by a signature, and should not override validation evidence.",
 "research_notes": "Evidence status after discovery batch: named markers feature_007, feature_058, feature_015 and their signature interactions are not supported. H12 (feature_003 vs0) is borderline and active: signed estimate 0.139, CI 0.065-0.213, below 0.15 threshold but compatible with threshold. Independent validation of H12 requested to control multiplicity and resolve borderline magnitude. Follow-up proposals are deliberately limited: if validation supports H12, inspect direct subgroup mean differences for feature_003 within feature_058=1, feature_007=1, feature_015=1, feature_038>=0.5, age>=60, and one feature_038 interaction. Direct subgroup claims should require the subgroup estimate and interval to exceed 0.15 in the claimed direction, not merely point below threshold. If H12 validation is null/subthreshold, close the feature_003 line and broaden to untested categorical predictors, but apply stricter interpretation due to multiplicity. Do not revive null named-marker interactions unless validation or a new independent finding strongly supports them.",
 "validate": "H12"
